---
import site from '../data/site.json';

const glam2Label = `$${site.glam2_cost_usd.toFixed(2)}`;
const costLabel = `$${site.cost_usd.toFixed(2)}`;
const millipore = site.millipore_cost_usd.toLocaleString('en-US');
---
<section id="background">
  <div class="eyebrow">Background</div>
  <h2>Background</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    Membrane filtration for <em>E. coli</em> is the measurement WHO and
    UNICEF use in household drinking-water quality surveys. Wider testing
    is limited by access to the instrument that performs the measurement.
  </p>

  <div class="stat-row">
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="num">{site.context.population_without_safe_water_bn} bn</div>
      <div class="label">people without safely managed drinking water</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="num">{site.context.population_without_water_quality_data_pct} %</div>
      <div class="label">of the global population lacks any water-quality data</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Surveying water quality at many sites requires many instruments, so
    the number of units available matters more than the performance of
    any single one. The steel Millipore EZ-Fit manifold costs
    approximately ${millipore.toString()} per unit. It is the reference
    instrument 3DPLAM was validated against. The EZ-Fit is manufactured
    centrally from a closed design, so it can be purchased but not
    produced locally.
  </p>
  <p>
    UNICEF's second-generation lightweight affordable manifold (2GLAM)
    reduces the per-unit price to approximately {glam2Label}. 2GLAM is
    still produced centrally from a proprietary design, so its
    availability stays tied to the same supply chain. At approximately
    {costLabel} per set, 3DPLAM costs only modestly less. Its main
    difference is that the design is open and can be 3D-printed locally.
    Anyone with an FDM printer can produce and modify it without
    depending on a supply chain.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .stat-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 20px;
    margin: 24px 0 28px;
  }
  .stat {
    padding: 20px 22px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .stat .num {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 32px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .stat .label {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    line-height: 1.45;
    max-width: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .stat-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
